WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.535
A good example of 
what a WHY sounds like

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:05.388
I'll tell you a story

00:00:05.388 --> 00:00:09.100
I did some work with the Disney Imagineers

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.040
these are the people who 
build all the rides,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.521
design all the parades,

00:00:12.521 --> 00:00:14.067
all the shows, the boats,

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.920
everything like that.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.528
Everything that's not a movie or
merchandising basically

00:00:19.528 --> 00:00:23.387
the Imagineers 
invent it, build it, design it.

00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:26.060
And I was giving a talk about

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.600
the WHY 
and the Golden Circle to the Imagineers

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.480
and somebody asked the same question
which is

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.440
"Can you give us an example of 
what a WHY looks like

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:33.080
or sounds like?"

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.392
So I picked a random person 
in the audience

00:00:36.392 --> 00:00:38.396
and I asked him to give me

00:00:38.396 --> 00:00:41.600
a specific story 
that helps me understand,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.300
that really captures 
what he loves

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.800
about being an Imagineer.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.840
And he told a story 
you have to appreciate

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.500
that he told over the course of 
seven minutes maybe

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.900
basically of how he was the
lead engineer on a ride

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.000
and he went to

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.199
I should preempt with,
I should tell you this

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.213
that he didn't know this

00:01:05.213 --> 00:01:06.900
and I found out later

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.000
that his nickname at the office was
"ice chips"

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.500
because he was cold and everything

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.299
well he's an engineer 
so everything was exact

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:17.483
and just sort of not the most
emotional guy

00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:18.900
so they called him Ice Chips

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.119
this was his nickname behind his back.

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:24.580
So I called on Ice Chips by accident and

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.490
he told the story of how

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.000
there was a new ride that was opening

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.860
that he was the lead engineer and

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.950
he saw a guy in a wheelchair 
and his daughter

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.350
heading towards the ride

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.000
to try it out for the first time

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.640
and one of
the things that occurred to him was that

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.200
anywhere else in the world

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.610
people see
a guy in a wheelchair with his daughter.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.900
Only at Disneyland 
the only thing people see

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.500
is a father and his daughter
going to Disneyland.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.400
And and he says 
that's what it means to him

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.232
to work for this organization.

00:02:01.232 --> 00:02:03.900
That it's about parents and children 
and family

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.252
and brothers and sisters

00:02:05.252 --> 00:02:06.674
and boyfriends and girlfriends

00:02:06.674 --> 00:02:07.957
and husbands and wives and

00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:10.720
every combination of family 
that we can come up with

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.500
and that's all there is

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.500
just those relationships.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.400
And that's why

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.160
everything was so exact to him.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.980
And in an instant we're all crying 
and it was a beautiful story

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.295
but in an instant
everybody understood

00:02:21.295 --> 00:02:23.180
why he was always so hard about everything

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.457
because to him
those were the stakes.

00:02:25.457 --> 00:02:29.300
They had to make things
that made people feel

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:32.410
that they were just a father and a daughter

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.780
that nothing else mattered.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.200
It was pretty amazing.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.170
And it gave everybody context

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.800
everybody fell in love with him that day.

